WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.250
Here is the learning path for this module We will
approach SQL

00:00:04.262 --> 00:00:08.450
gradually instead of trying to learn everything at
once We begin with

00:00:08.462 --> 00:00:12.825
reading data You will use SELECT to choose columns
FROM to identify

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.312
the table WHERE to filter rows ORDER BY to sort
results and

00:00:16.337 --> 00:00:20.262
LIMIT to restrict how many rows are displayed We
will also use

00:00:20.288 --> 00:00:25.412
aliases and simple expressions so the output is
easier to understand Next

00:00:25.575 --> 00:00:31.588
we move to changing data INSERT adds new rows UPDATE
changes existing

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:37.162
rows DELETE can remove rows These commands are
powerful so we

00:00:37.175 --> 00:00:41.825
will combine them with verification steps instead of
running them casually The

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:46.125
third part is protection We will use stable
identifiers such as a

00:00:46.138 --> 00:00:49.800
primary key or a unique MRN transactions that can be
committed or

00:00:49.825 --> 00:00:55.350
rolled back database constraints and PostgreSQL's
RETURNING clause These tools

00:00:55.375 --> 00:00:59.838
help us see exactly what was affected The coding
progression is also

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:05.638
gradual First run a complete example Second change
one small

00:01:05.662 --> 00:01:10.862
part and compare the output Third complete a missing
operator value or

00:01:10.888 --> 00:01:15.525
clause Fourth write a short statement using an
earlier example as a

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:21.262
pattern The goal is understanding not memorization
If you understand

00:01:21.288 --> 00:01:23.688
what each clause is doing and can adapt a pattern to
a

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.275
new question you are learning SQL the right way
